### SLE GWAS
### European ancestry

The European SLE GWAS comprised four contributing cohorts:

| Cohort | Cases | Controls | Total N | Reference |

| GENENTECH | 1,163 | 2,106 | 3,269 | PMID: 21362770 |
| GWAS_WYSE | 4,036 | 6,959 | 10,995 | PMID: 26502338 |
| SLE_EUR_GSA | 1,183 | 6,821 | 8,004 | Unpublished |
| SLEGEN | 522 | 2,543 | 3,065 | PMID: 18204446 |

Total: 6,904 cases, 18,429 controls (N = 25,333).

### East Asian ancestry

The East Asian SLE GWAS included 13 contributing cohorts from China, Hong Kong, Japan, South Korea and Thailand.

Total: 18,212 cases, 256,625 controls (N = 274,837).

### Trans-ancestry meta-analysis

The combined SLE meta-analysis included:

- Cases: 25,116
- Controls: 275,054
- Total N: 300,170

Genome build: GRCh38


